# Fleet inventory — one host per line.
# Format:  name  ip  groups[,comma,separated]  [user]
#   - name    : short alias used by the `fleet` CLI and ssh/config
#   - ip       : reachable address (these are Tailscale 100.x addresses)
#   - groups   : comma-separated tags; every host is implicitly in `all`
#   - user     : (optional) ssh user for this host; overrides FLEET_SSH_USER
#
# Columns are whitespace-separated. Lines starting with # are ignored.
# Edit groups/users to match reality. Keep this file in git (no secrets here).
#
# Location/provider tags added 2026-08-17 from a measured survey — see
# docs/cloud-inventory.md. `cloud` vs `onprem` is the split that matters for
# the cloud-exit work; `contabo`/`ovh` map 1:1 to billing lines.
#
# name            ip                groups                              user
aiapi             100.87.7.40       manager,cloud,contabo,all
vps-custmer       100.64.137.68     vps,cloud,ovh,all
vpscld            100.99.240.28     vps,cloud,contabo,all
vps-gra6          100.101.47.112    vps,cloud,ovh,all
vpsall            100.68.77.46      vps,cloud,ovh,offline,all
vps-office        100.85.35.45      vps,cloud,ovh,all
openwebui-vps     100.115.82.76     vps,app,cloud,ovh,vm-on-storai,all
nerve-hub         100.89.89.47      app,cloud,contabo,all
arcai             100.81.132.108    app,cloud,ovh,baremetal,all
vps-dioneto       100.106.171.90    vps,cloud,ovh,vm-on-storai,all
storai            100.92.89.14      storage,hypervisor,cloud,ovh,baremetal,all
dgxmain           100.124.217.84    dgx,gpu,onprem,arm64,all
dgxsec            100.78.185.72     dgx,gpu,onprem,arm64,all
5060ihome         100.90.81.47      gpu,home,onprem,all
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Known machines deliberately NOT enabled above (would change `fleet run all`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# bit001          194.146.12.114    manager,cloud,contabo   # the MCP hub this
#                   agent connects THROUGH. Managing it via the fleet CLI while
#                   it proxies the fleet is a foot-gun; drive it directly.
#
# c001            100.79.164.8      cloud,unknown   # online, tag:hub in
#                   Tailscale, our fleet key is rejected. Identify before use.
# meni-office0    100.103.133.48    office,unknown  # online, key rejected.
# nitay           (NAT on storai)   cloud,ovh,vm-on-storai  # nitay.yohay.ai,
#                   no Tailscale node of its own — reach via storai/virsh.
# df001-brn       84.247.130.13     cloud,contabo   # serves df001.yohay.ai
#                   (Dify) + brn.yohay.ai. HTTP/HTTPS up, SSH closed, no access.
# (dead)          162.19.126.209    cloud,ovh       # all ports closed; 12 stale
#                   yohay.ai DNS records still point here.
#
# Notes on entries above:
#   - `vpsall` is a powered-off VM on storai, not an independent VPS. Its
#     cloudflared tunnels show healthy because the connector runs on
#     openwebui-vps.
#   - `arcai` carried a `gpu` tag but has no GPU (nvidia-smi returns nothing);
#     tag removed.
#   - `openwebui-vps`, `vps-dioneto`, `nitay`, `vpsall` are all guests on
#     `storai`. Powering off storai takes all four with it.
